hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"15941","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, Abu Mu'awiya, meaning Shayban, narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Yahya ibn Ishaq, from Mujashi' ibn Mas'ud: that he brought a nephew of his to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge to him upon hijra. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, rather he pledges upon Islam, for there is no hijra after the conquest, and he will be of the followers in goodness."
"15942","Bakr ibn Isa narrated to us, he said, Abu Awana narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Mujashi' ibn Mas'ud, he said: I set out with my brother Ma'bad to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after the conquest, and said: O Messenger of Allah, pledge him upon hijra. So he said: Hijra has passed for its people. He said: So I said, then what? He said: Upon Islam and jihad."
"15943","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said, Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Yahya ibn Ishaq, that he informed him, from Mujashi' ibn Mas'ud al-Bahzi: that he brought his nephew to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to pledge him upon hijra. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: No, rather he pledges upon Islam, for there is no hijra after the conquest. He said: And he will be of the followers in goodness."
"15944","Affan narrated to us, Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, he said, Khalid al-Hadhdha narrated to us, from Abu Uthman, from Mujashi' ibn Mas'ud, he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, this is Mujalid ibn Mas'ud pledging you upon hijra. He said: There is no hijra after the conquest of Makka, but I pledge him upon Islam."
"15945","Ahmad ibn Abd al-Malik ibn Waqid narrated to us, he said, Zuhayr narrated to us, he said, Asim al-Ahwal narrated to us, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Mujashi', he said: I came with my brother Ma'bad to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after the conquest, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have brought you my brother to pledge him upon hijra. So he said: The people of hijra have gone with what is in it. So I said: Upon what do you pledge him? He said: Upon Islam and faith and jihad. He said: I met Ma'bad afterwards, and he was the elder of the two, so I asked him, and he said: Mujashi' spoke the truth."
